WHY THIS MATTERS FOR KSAV
-------------------------

There was no licence here at all until now, which under copyright law means
all rights reserved: nobody could legally use, fork or redistribute the work,
and the open-sourcing that spec.md names as the answer to the bus factor was
foreclosed. A permissive licence is also the consistent choice —
engine/src/spell/hebrew.rs rejects Hspell partly *because* it is AGPL, and it
would be strange to refuse a copyleft dependency and then ship one.


